1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
A phone is running a 7-step AI task.
A laptop on the same Wi-Fi is waiting.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Handoff while step 3 is running.
The phone lets go only after the laptop confirms it saved the task.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,500
The laptop re-runs step 3 under the SAME key,
so nothing is skipped.

4
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:33,500
The phone's own copy of step 3 finishes late and is sent over.
The laptop compares: the answers differ, so it flags it and stores both.

5
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:39,833
Steps 4 to 7 run on the laptop (sped up).

6
00:00:39,833 --> 00:00:48,833
The finished result comes back to the phone.

7
00:00:48,833 --> 00:00:51,833
Proof of concept: two devices, offline, no server.
At-least-once, not exactly-once.

